{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T09:22:22.425Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6da2f5f4d31f8f762cde8c96","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-thbdxu"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Expected revisions advance from the pre-override document when an item_store_write override transforms contents"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found in Codex review round 22 of PR #1654 (pm-gh1576). When a supported item_store_write extension override changes the persisted contents (for example a description-only transform), mutateItem advances the revision scope with its pre-override afterDocument. That hash does not describe the stored item, so a second guarded write in the same withExpectedItemRevisions scope (or a multi-write CLI command such as claim --start) refuses with item_revision_conflict although no other writer ran. It fails closed: a false refusal, never a lost update. advanceItemMutationPreconditions in core/store/item-mutation-precondition.ts receives the document from the item-store write path before the override result is known. Fix direction: advance from the persisted snapshot under the item lock (re-read or the override's returned contents), accounting for overrides that skip the write or delete, or refuse an incompatible override for a guarded write before committing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["expected-revision","extensions","pm-gh1576","storage-override"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-03T09:22:22.425Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T09:22:22.425Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A guarded scope that writes the same item twice under a contents-transforming item_store_write override admits both writes; A skipped or delete-converted override write advances the scope to the stored state (or refuses before commit), with a spec for each; A competing peer write between the two guarded writes still refuses with item_revision_conflict"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Under a contents-transforming item_store_write override, a guarded scope advances to the revision actually persisted, so its own next write is admitted and only a competing write refuses."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The scope advances to the pre-override document hash, so its own next guarded write refuses with item_revision_conflict."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1576","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-03T09:22:22.425Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9a6c7bbf119ec1afff1a56727700e2d11c7b2a57fcfb916eab55ef51c538e375","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":